8	/**
9	 * The single, consolidated duplicate check for {@code POST /api/owners}: rejects the request with
10	 * 409 when the new owner's whole {@link OwnerIdentityKey identityKey}
11	 * ({@code normalizedTelephone|email|householdId}) equals an existing owner's. This replaces the
12	 * former separate telephone, email and household checks; because the telephone is part of the key,
13	 * two members of one household (same householdId) with different telephones have different keys and
14	 * are both allowed — only an exact full-key match is a duplicate.
15	 *
16	 * <p>Runs after {@link AssignHouseholdId} so the householdId segment is populated before the key is
17	 * built, and before {@link SaveOwner} so the not-yet-saved owner is not compared against itself.
18	 */
